            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SpeedyMilk3002"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Our favorite cocktail is a Paloma- grapefruit juice and tequila- so this recipe was a find. Rubbed the chicken with poultry seasoning and chili and rested uncovered in fridge overnight. Stuffed with quartered grapefruit and made a quick dressing from olive oil and grapefruit juice to baste after roasting @ 425 for 30 minutes, then turning down to 350 degrees, basting and rotating (on rack) every 30 mins or so until 165 on thermometer. Served with cornbread spiked with jalapenos and a rice pilaf with lemon and zucchini... plenty of roasting juice and Palomas.",
            "datePublished": "2026-07-28T22:04:25.425Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lisa McCarthy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My new favorite roasted chicken! So flavorful! I marinated it overnight. I added rosemary, garlic and onion the marinade just because. I started it off breast side down. Halfway through I turned it over. Browning the breast. So juicy and tender!",
            "datePublished": "2020-05-11T23:52:55.190Z"
          },
          {
